Package: htebalance
Type: Package
Title: Diagnosing Subgroup Imbalance and HTE Sensitivity
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Songeun Emily", "Lee", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "selee4@uh.edu")
Description: Before reporting treatment effects for prespecified subgroups in
    randomized experiments, researchers can check how much information each
    group provides and how sensitive their conclusions are to the choice of
    estimator. The package reports subgroup sizes, shares, treated and control
    cell counts, effective sample sizes, difference-in-means estimates with
    standard errors and minimum detectable effects; compares group average
    treatment effects and between-group contrasts across subgroup means,
    interacted OLS, causal forests, and BART; and writes a plain-language
    summary of the results. Small subgroup size and small subgroup share are
    reported separately.
